{"key":"XamlGorpWindow","text":"## XamlGorpWindow\n\nThe **XAML Gorp Window** is the full XAML visual designer (everything the\n**XAML Window** does) plus a Gorp palette and a one-click **Execute** that\nruns the design's Gorp logic against the backend. See the **XamlWindow**\nhelp for the core designer; this section covers the Gorp additions.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.03 | \">\" toggles the standard control palette, \"<\" toggles the Gorp palette, and Execute runs the Gorp algorithm. An API status label shows Executing / SUCCESS / Error.\nGorp Palette | 0.04, 0.50 | Gorp-specific tiles — drag one onto the canvas (hover a tile for its description).\nCanvas | 0.50, 0.45 | The same visual XAML editing as the XAML Window — select, drag, resize, edit properties.\nResult Display | 0.50, 0.90 | Shows the backend computation result after you press Execute.\n\n---\n\n### Gorp additions\n\n- **Execute** — send the current design's Gorp logic to the backend and show the result\n- **>** — toggle the standard WPF control palette\n- **<** — toggle the Gorp palette\n- **API status** — Executing (yellow) → SUCCESS (green) or Error (red)\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- Same editing keys as the XAML Window: **Ctrl/Cmd + C / X / V / D**, **Delete / Backspace**\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: AIDesign","screenshot":""}